{number: 135}
{title: I am Coming to the Cross}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] I am coming to the cross;
I am [F] poor, and weak, and [C] blind;
I am counting all but dross,
I shall [G7] full salvation [C] find.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C] I am trusting, Lord, in Thee,
Blessed [F] Lamb of Calva-[C] ry;
Humbly at Thy cross I bow,
Save me, [G7] Jesus, save me [C] now.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Long my heart has sighed for Thee,
Long has [F] evil reigned with-[C] in;
Jesus sweetly speaks to me:
"I will [G7] cleanse you from all [C] sin."
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Here I give my all to Thee,
Friends, and [F] time, and earthly [C] store;
Soul and body Thine to be,
Wholly [G7] Thine for ever-[C] more.
{end_of_verse}
